*

# The build context for BOTH images is the repository root, so everything the
# Dockerfiles read is repo-relative and only two trees are re-included here:
# deps/ (the offline payload) and docker/ (the image assets).

# --- offline payload: bind-mounted, never COPYed ---------------------------
# deps/ carries the CANN .run, the AArch64 wheelhouse, the local apt archive
# and the vllm-ascend source. It is mounted at build time, never copied, so it
# costs no image layer.
!deps
# ...but not the parts no Dockerfile reads. The vLLM source is only needed
# while provisioning builds its wheel, and .provision is scratch space.
deps/src/vllm
deps/.provision

# --- image assets ----------------------------------------------------------
# docker/target-310p/     Dockerfile.aarch64 plus the package lists, patches,
#                         entrypoint and verification script it mounts or COPYs
# docker/builder-x86_64/  the cross-compilation Dockerfile plus the sysroot
#                         assembly and verification scripts it COPYs
!docker
